Pyro LTO patch: with LTO_MODE, the interpreter unit is compiled without LTO.

IPInt::initialize() checks that the offlineasm handlers in llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp sit exactly
alignIPInt bytes apart. With -flto the unit's inline asm is emitted by the LTO backend at link time,
which breaks that layout: the RELEASE_ASSERT kills the process at startup. The GCC postprocess-asm
path already builds this unit without LTO; clang now does too. Builds without LTO_MODE (the default)
are unchanged. scripts/jsc/build.sh applies it on top of patches/ for PYRO_JSC_LTO builds only, so
it is not part of the cache key of the default build (scripts/jsc/cache-key.sh).

diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/CMakeLists.txt b/Source/JavaScriptCore/CMakeLists.txt
index 7a04bb8a1e..72c8164ad8 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1827,6 +1827,14 @@ add_dependencies(JavaScriptCore_CopyPrivateHeaders Bytecodes JSCBuiltins JSCWebP
 target_include_directories(LowLevelInterpreterLib
     PRIVATE "$<TARGET_PROPERTY:JavaScriptCore,INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES>" "${JavaScriptCore_PRIVATE_FRAMEWORK_HEADERS_DIR}/JavaScriptCore")
 add_dependencies(LowLevelInterpreterLib Bytecodes JSCBuiltins JSCWebPreferenceOptions)
+
+if (LTO_MODE AND COMPILER_IS_CLANG)
+    # IPInt::initialize() validates that its opcode handlers in the offlineasm output sit
+    # exactly alignIPInt bytes apart. The LTO backend emits that inline asm at link time and
+    # breaks the layout (RELEASE_ASSERT -> SIGKILL on startup), so the interpreter unit is
+    # compiled without LTO, as the GCC postprocess-asm path below already does.
+    set_source_files_properties("llint/LowLevelInterpreter.cpp" PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS "-fno-lto")
+endif ()
 if (TARGET WTF_CopyHeaders)
     add_dependencies(LowLevelInterpreterLib WTF_CopyHeaders)
 endif ()
